    "explanation": "To the driver and to the rider: this dispute is decided on the fare record and the GPS trace, and it leaves both of you where you already are.\n\nThe driver's request — that the SGD 3.00 ERP line be released to him — cannot be granted. The SGD 3.00 is the 'Canal Corridor entry' charge. The fare breakdown records it as on the optimal route, and the GPS trace passes the gantry at a nearest-fix distance of 0.0 m at 16:24:40, so it is a real crossing of a real on-route gantry, properly chargeable as a government pass-through under POL-RD-09. No clause turns an ERP pass-through into a payment to the driver: POL-RD-04 driver compensation requires the rider to have been billed for more than 1.0 km less than the trace records, and here the ledger bills 11.0 km against an 11.0 km trace — no shortfall — while POL-RD-12 applies only to RYDE_POOL trips and this was a RYDE_X trip. POL-RD-11(a) fixes an UPFRONT_QUOTE rider's remedy at charged_total 26.00 less quoted_fare 23.00 less the properly chargeable pass-through of 3.00, which is exactly the 0.00 the ledger publishes as pol_rd_11_remedy: nothing is owing from this fare to either party.\n\nThere is likewise no deviation to refund to the rider or to charge to the driver. The governing trace figure is 11.0 km under POL-RD-01, against an optimal of 11.2 km — an excess of -0.2 km, or -1.8%. Both establishment tests fail (the excess must exceed 0.8 km and 20% of optimal), and re-running the test on the amended endpoints under POL-RD-05 gives the same amended optimal of 11.2 km / 20.0 min and the same negative excess, so POL-RD-05's own direction is NO_ACTION. The destination amendment is timestamped 16:27:40, after the gantry was charged at 16:24:40, so it neither created nor removed the ERP line.\n\nThe rider's point that the amended baseline leaves the gantry unverified is rejected: the trace crossed the gantry on the route as actually driven at 16:24:40, before the amendment, and the line is flagged on the optimal route. There is no traffic advisory on file (EV-ADVIS-00709-01 is missing, weight 0.0), and because no party asserts an external traffic cause, POL-RD-03 has no advisory to run against and plays no part.\n\nThe outcome is NO_ACTION: the fare stands, payment_status remains PENDING and refund_issued_sgd remains 0.00, left exactly as they are. No money moves to either party, and no referral is produced — there is no material deviation and no repeat-pattern finding for a POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral, and no phantom or off-route line for a POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral."
