    "explanation": "To both parties: the record is agreed and it does not support moving any money in this dispute. This was an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip — quoted fare SGD 23.00, charged total SGD 26.00, the difference being the single SGD 3.00 'Canal Corridor entry' ERP line.\n\nThere is no route deviation. The GPS trace governs the distance under POL-RD-01 (trace_distance_km 11.0 km) against the booked optimal of 11.2 km, an excess of -0.2 km, or -1.79%. Neither establishment test is met (the excess must exceed 0.8 km in absolute terms AND 20% of optimal), so no deviation exists and nothing is refundable on distance or time. The rider's destination amendment at 16:27:40 re-bases that test under POL-RD-05 to the amended optimal of 11.2 km / 20.0 min; driving 11.0 km against 11.2 km again yields no excess, and POL-RD-05 directs NO_ACTION where no deviation survives. On an upfront-quoted trip POL-RD-02 does not run in any event (POL-RD-11).\n\nThe SGD 3.00 ERP line is properly chargeable, not phantom or off-route. The fare_breakdown records it on_optimal_route true, and the trace passes the gantry at a nearest-fix distance of 0.0 m at 16:24:40, well inside POL-RD-09's 250 m match radius. POL-RD-09(4)'s billing-integrity refund reaches only a gantry the trace never passes, so it does not fire and no referral arises. The gantry was crossed at 16:24:40, three minutes before the rider's 16:27:40 change, so POL-RD-09(3) also gives no ERP refund. Under POL-RD-11 the rider's remedy is charged_total 26.00 less quoted fare 23.00 less properly chargeable pass-throughs 3.00 = SGD 0.00, exactly the published pol_rd_11_remedy of 0.00.\n\nThe driver's request to have the SGD 3.00 released to him is not a remedy any clause creates. POL-RD-09 characterises an ERP charge as a third-party, government-set pass-through settled separately from distance and time charges; the clauses that can move money to a driver are POL-RD-04 and POL-RD-12. POL-RD-04's compensation limb fails because the ledger bills 11.0 km against an 11.0 km trace, so there is no unbilled-distance shortfall exceeding 1.0 km to pay at SGD 0.75/km, and POL-RD-12 does not apply because the vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL. The rider's argument that the line's on_optimal_route flag does not say which optimal route it was assessed against does not change this: the line is matched to the trace at 0.0 m and remains properly chargeable, and no refundable amount would arise either way. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00709-01, MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) is citable as an absence, but nothing turns on it because no party asserts an external traffic cause.\n\nBecause the driver filed this dispute and the evidence does not support his claim, the outcome is NO_ACTION: the present state stands. refund_issued_sgd remains 0.00 and the payment status remains PENDING — no amount is refunded to the rider and none is released to the driver. Nothing in this case produces a referral."
